---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHORS, SITE } from '../data/taxonomy';
import { getPosts, postUrl, abs } from '../lib/site';
import { ORG_ID } from '../lib/schema';
const posts = await getPosts();
const desk = AUTHORS.desk;
const profile = {
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  url: abs('/authors/'),
  name: 'Authors',
  mainEntity: { '@type': 'Organization', name: desk.name, description: desk.bio, parentOrganization: { '@id': ORG_ID }, email: SITE.email },
};
---
<Base title="Authors" description="Who writes Quetzal Review, and how stories are researched, sourced and updated." crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Authors', path: '/authors/' }]} extraSchema={[profile]}>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Authors</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="desk">{desk.name}</h2>
      <p class="meta">{desk.role}</p>
      <p>{desk.bio}</p>
      <p>Stories are written in a warm, story-led voice, but they are researched rather than lived: the editors do not claim first-hand experiences in their writing, and every fact that affects your safety, health, entry requirements or budget is linked to its source. When we add named contributors, each will have a profile here describing their own experience of Guatemala.</p>
      <p>Write to the editors at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
      <h3>Stories by the editors</h3>
      <ul>
        {posts.filter((p) => p.data.author === 'desk').map((p) => <li><a href={postUrl(p)}>{p.data.title}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
